        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-merchant-of-venice/sceneII_22.8/p@65314",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SOLANIO.\nI never heard a passion so confus’d,\nSo strange, outrageous, and so variable\nAs the dog Jew did utter in the streets.\n“My daughter! O my ducats! O my daughter!\nFled with a Christian! O my Christian ducats!\nJustice! the law! my ducats and my daughter!\nA sealed bag, two sealed bags of ducats,\nOf double ducats, stol’n from me by my daughter!\nAnd jewels, two stones, two rich and precious stones,\nStol’n by my daughter! Justice! find the girl,\nShe hath the stones upon her and the ducats.”",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-merchant-of-venice/sceneII_22.8/p@65314/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
